-- title:
--   Surjectivity of the residue field map under base change
-- statement:
--   Let $P$, $X$, $T$, $S$ be schemes (in a fixed universe) together with morphisms $\mathrm{fst} : P \to X$, $\mathrm{snd} : P \to T$, $f : X \to S$ and $g : T \to S$, and assume `H` expresses that the square formed by these four morphisms is a pullback square, i.e. $\mathrm{fst}$ followed by $f$ equals $\mathrm{snd}$ followed by $g$ and $(P,\mathrm{fst},\mathrm{snd})$ is a limit of the cospan $X \to S \leftarrow T$. Let $t$ be a point of the underlying topological space of $P$, and assume, as a typeclass hypothesis, that the induced map of residue fields $f.\mathrm{residueFieldMap}$ at the point $\mathrm{fst}(t)$ of $X$, that is $\kappa(f(\mathrm{fst}(t))) \to \kappa(\mathrm{fst}(t))$, is an isomorphism in the category of commutative rings. The conclusion is that the underlying ring homomorphism of the residue field map induced by $\mathrm{snd}$ at $t$, namely $\kappa(\mathrm{snd}(t)) \to \kappa(t)$, is a surjective function. (Surjectivity is asserted; since both sides are fields and the map is a ring homomorphism between them, this amounts to its being an isomorphism, but only surjectivity is stated.)
--
--   This is the standard description of residue fields of points of a fibre product: a point of $P$ over $x \in X$ and $y \in T$ with common image $s \in S$ has residue field a quotient of a localisation of $\kappa(x) \otimes_{\kappa(s)} \kappa(y)$, so when $\kappa(s) \to \kappa(x)$ is an isomorphism the residue field of the point is generated by that of $y$. It is used in the construction of charts for the base change of the Deligne–Rapoport style model, where it forces the residue field at a base-changed point to agree with that of its image.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_IsPullback_surjective_residueFieldMap_of_isIso_residueFieldMap.lean

